@*
    "Prism" as a written signature for the sign-in page (Areas/Identity/Pages/Account/Login.cshtml).
    Inline SVG, so it ships with the app and needs no font file: the letter shapes are the
    outlines of Dancing Script Bold (SIL Open Font License 1.1), and each .auth__sig-stroke
    is a pen path drawn down the middle of one stroke, in writing order (the P's stem, its
    bowl, "ris" joined, "m", then the dot of the i).
    At rest only the solid word shows. In the opening sequence auth-login.css draws the pen
    paths in turn inside the mask, which uncovers the spectrum-filled word as if written,
    and then fades the solid word in over it. The mask paths are white because a mask reads
    brightness; nothing else here sets a colour. Ids are fixed, so render it once per page.
*@
